    {
      "id": 40,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -680,
        0
      ],
      "size": [
        640,
        1000
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 39,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## FLUX.2 [dev]: inpainting, references\n\nRepaints the masked area of an image with FLUX.2 [dev] (not an inpaint model: the masked latent is re-noised and\nsampled with the rest of the image as context). **Differential Diffusion** makes a soft (feathered) mask blend\ngradually; the result is pasted back through the original mask, so nothing outside it changes.\n\n## Image Bench\n\nThe Generate tab is in **Inpaint** mode while this workflow is loaded.\n\n| Marker | Node | Generate tab |\n|--------|------|--------------|\n| `ib:img` | Load Image | Input cell; \"Send image\" from Photoshop |\n| `ib:mask` | Load Image Mask | Mask cell; the Photoshop selection |\n| `ib:cp`, `ib:pp`, `ib:lora` | as in the other workflows | model, prompt, LoRAs |\n| `ib:smp` | SamplerCustomAdvanced | seed, steps, sampling method, Distilled CFG, denoising (Denoise) |\n| `ib:ref:0-3` | Reference 1-4 (bypassed) | References panel |\n\nThe loaders refer to the files the Photoshop plugin writes (`image_bench_photoshop_*.png`); send an image and a\nmask, or set them in the Input / Mask cells of the Generate tab, before the first queue.\n\n- Describe the **whole image**, including the new content of the masked area.\n- Denoising 0.85-1.0 replaces the content, 0.4-0.7 keeps its colors and shapes.\n- The image keeps its size (the scheduler reads it); keep the sides multiples of 16 and within 0.5-4 MP.\n- A reference (for instance the object to put into the masked area) is used as in text-to-image.\n\n**References** (up to 4; FLUX.2 [dev] takes up to 10, add slots by copying a column and numbering its\nloader `ib:ref:4`, ...): add images in the References panel of the Generate tab (a tab next to LoRA), by\n\"Ps sends to: reference\" from Photoshop, or by dropping them there. An empty slot is bypassed together with its\nscale and encode nodes; its **Reference Latent** stays and passes the conditioning on unchanged. Refer to the\nreferences by order in the prompt (*\"the woman from image 1 wearing the jacket from image 2\"*). Each is scaled\nto 1 MP first.\n\n## Model Links\n\n**diffusion_models**: [flux2_dev_fp8mixed.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/flux2-dev/resolve/main/split_files/diffusion_models/flux2_dev_fp8mixed.safetensors)\n**text_encoders**: [mistral_3_small_flux2_bf16.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/flux2-dev/resolve/main/split_files/text_encoders/mistral_3_small_flux2_bf16.safetensors)\n**vae**: [full_encoder_small_decoder.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/black-forest-labs/FLUX.2-small-decoder/resolve/main/full_encoder_small_decoder.safetensors)\n"
      ],
      "title": "Note: FLUX.2 [dev] inpainting (Image Bench)",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
